# ClawAI — Cursor rules (pointer)

Read AGENTS.md first: it is the canonical router for every agent (identity,
authority order, first command, landing a change, prohibitions, where everything
lives). Cursor-specific notes: cursor.md.

Before editing, run:
  npm run knowledge:context -- --task="<task>"
and read .ai/local/current-context.md.

Before you finish any change, update every doc it makes stale (rule 63). The
hooks will reject it otherwise.

Akinator runs on EVERY change with no command typed: ask, resolve, audit, plan, implement,
document, skillify, rule, contextify, memoize, index+sync, verify. Read skills/akinator/SKILL.md
(rules/65). A new flagship, core or big feature ships its public marketing page in the same
change (rules/66, skills/ship-a-feature-marketing-page.md).

Land a change through the hooks — never bypass them:
  git add <explicit paths>  ->  git commit (Docs: trailer)  ->  git push
What each hook runs: rules/23-git-commits-hooks-and-release-gates.md (gate matrix).

Blockers: rules/00-non-negotiable-rules.md. Testing is 15 QA lanes with a
docs/qa-evidence record (QA-WORKFLOW.md, rules/60). User-facing text needs i18n in
all 13 locales (rules/20).

Delegated agents and models (rule 64): smallest fast model only for read-only audit/context
agents; strong model for code and QA; never a flagship or max effort; ask the owner when
unsure. See rules/64-subagent-model-selection.md.
